      "time": 1793212814.534796,
      "body": "@OpenCode I am working in exercises/10-marginal-effect-exercise.ipynb, with R and tidymodels.\nI already ran the cells that make these objects:\n\n- fit_logit: a tidymodels logistic_reg() model, fit with grass ~ educ.\n  grass is a factor with levels \"no\" and \"yes\".\n- grass_by_educ: a table with two columns, educ and grass.\n  grass is the share of people who said yes at each education level.\n\nPut R code in the empty code cell in step 3 that:\n\n1. Makes a grid with educ = 0:20.\n2. Predicts on the grid with fit_logit and type = 'prob', and binds the grid to the predictions.\n3. Plots the grass_by_educ points with educ on the x-axis, and draws .pred_yes as a line on top.\n\nThen run the cell. Use tidymodels only. Do not load other packages.\nDo not change any other cells.",
      "type": "msg"
    },
    {
      "body": "@OpenCode I am working in exercises/10-marginal-effect-exercise.ipynb, with R and tidymodels.\nI already ran the cells that make these objects:\n\n- fit_logit: a tidymodels logistic_reg() model, fit with grass ~ educ.\n  grass is a factor with levels \"no\" and \"yes\".\n- grass_by_educ: a table with two columns, educ and grass.\n  grass is the share of people who said yes at each education level.\n- preds: predicts on a grid of educ from 0 to 20 years with fit_logit and type = 'prob', and binds the grid to the predictions.\n\nPut R code in the empty code cell in step 3 that:\n\n1. Predicts the probability of yes at their own educ for each individual\n2. Predicts again at educ + 1\n3. Subtracts these two values to find the change in attitute toward marijuana with one additional education year, then takes the mean of this value of change over all individuals\n\nThen run the cell. Use tidymodels only. Do not load other packages.\nDo not change any other cells.",
      "time": 1793213002.1754348,
      "type": "msg",
      "id": "f40f66d4-6a60-4899-9760-73e9323d6253",
      "sender": "f251744eeda349039f0956b2692e9832",
      "metadata": {
