      "body": "@OpenCode I am working in exercises/11-challenger-exercise.ipynb, with R and tidymodels. The data frame challenger has a column temp (launch temperature, \u00b0F) and a column damage_f (a factor with levels \"no\" and \"yes\"). In the empty cell in step 4, Make a grid with temp = 30:85. Predict on the grid with type = 'prob' and bind the grid to the predictions. Then plot the jittered data with .pred_yes as a line on top. Add a vertical line at 31\u00b0F with geom_vline(xintercept = 31, linetype = 'dashed'). Do not change any other cells. ",
      "type": "msg"
    },
    {
      "time": 1793832090.1702669,
